PLAYER2 Android Native Audio Runtime
======================================

This project is the MKW standalone music player. Its audio engine is derived
from PLAYER2 (https://github.com/mylittleblover/player2-android-new), which is a
private repository owned by the same copyright holder as this project.

Authorization
=============

The repository owner (mylittleblover) explicitly authorized copying PLAYER2
source into this repository on 2026-11-07, choosing option B of three offered
options ("copy PLAYER2 sources into the new repository with an explicit license
and recorded authorization"). This file records that authorization.

Because the copyright holder of PLAYER2 and of this project is the same legal
person, no third-party grant is required for the PLAYER2 portions.

License status of this project
==============================

As of 2026-11-07 the project owner has NOT chosen a public distribution license.
The default is therefore: All Rights Reserved. No permission is granted to copy,
modify, or redistribute this project's own source code except by the copyright
holder.

If a public license is chosen later, it applies only to code owned by this
project and never overrides the third-party licenses listed below.

Third-party components
======================

These are used unmodified or with documented patches and carry their own terms.
Their notices must be preserved. See NOTICE-THIRD-PARTY.md for the full list and
app/src/main/assets/licenses/ for the redistributed texts.

  - clHCA (vgmstream)        ISC
  - libopenmpt               BSD-3-Clause
  - minimp3                  CC0 1.0 Universal
  - dr_flac / dr_mp3         MIT-0
  - stb_vorbis               MIT
  - Opus                     BSD-3-Clause
  - Game_Music_Emu           LGPL-2.1-or-later (built as a replaceable shared
                             library, gme_shared -> libgme.so)
  - Oboe                     Apache-2.0
  - AndroidX / Jetpack       Apache-2.0
  - Kotlin standard library  Apache-2.0

The LGPL Game_Music_Emu component is deliberately linked as a separate shared
object (libgme.so) so it stays replaceable, as LGPL requires.

No game assets are included
===========================

This repository contains no Nintendo audio, no .bars/.bwav/.bfstm files, and no
extracted game data. It is a player; the user supplies their own legally obtained
files at runtime. Nothing here circumvents a technical protection measure.
